{"entryType": "UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)", "primaryAccession": "Q6ZRH7", "secondaryAccessions": ["A6NEG6", "Q659E1"], "uniProtkbId": "CTSRG_HUMAN", "entryAudit": {"firstPublicDate": "2005-08-16", "lastAnnotationUpdateDate": "2026-06-10", "lastSequenceUpdateDate": "2008-11-25", "entryVersion": 146, "sequenceVersion": 3}, "annotationScore": 4.0, "organism": {"scientificName": "Homo sapiens", "commonName": "Human", "taxonId": 9606, "lineage": ["Eukaryota", "Metazoa", "Chordata", "Craniata", "Vertebrata", "Euteleostomi", "Mammalia", "Eutheria", "Euarchontoglires", "Primates", "Haplorrhini", "Catarrhini", "Hominidae", "Homo"]}, "proteinExistence": "1: Evidence at protein level", "proteinDescription": {"recommendedName": {"fullName": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000312", "source": "HGNC", "id": "HGNC:25243"}], "value": "Cation channel sperm-associated auxiliary subunit gamma"}}, "flag": "Precursor"}, "genes": [{"geneName": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000312", "source": "HGNC", "id": "HGNC:25243"}], "value": "CATSPERG"}, "synonyms": [{"value": "C19orf15"}]}], "comments": [{"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "C6KI89"}], "value": "Auxiliary component of the CatSper complex, a complex involved in sperm cell hyperactivation. Sperm cell hyperactivation is needed for sperm motility which is essential late in the preparation of sperm for fertilization"}], "commentType": "FUNCTION"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "C6KI89"}], "value": "Component of the CatSper complex or CatSpermasome composed of the core pore-forming members CATSPER1, CATSPER2, CATSPER3 and CATSPER4 as well as auxiliary members CATSPERB, CATSPERG, CATSPERD, CATSPERE, CATSPERZ, CATSPERT, CATSPERQ, CATSPERH and EFCAB9. HSPA1 may be an additional auxiliary complex member. The core complex members CATSPER1, CATSPER2, CATSPER3 and CATSPER4 form a heterotetrameric channel. The auxiliary CATSPERB, CATSPERG, CATSPERD and CATSPERE subunits form a pavilion-like structure over the pore which stabilizes the complex through interactions with CATSPER4, CATSPER3, CATSPER1 and CATSPER2 respectively. CATSPERH interacts with CATSPERB, further stabilizing the complex. CATSPERT interacts at least with CATSPERD and is required for targeting the CatSper complex in the flagellar membrane"}], "commentType": "SUBUNIT"}, {"commentType": "SUBCELLULAR LOCATION", "subcellularLocations": [{"location": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"}], "value": "Cell projection, cilium, flagellum membrane", "id": "SL-0115"}, "topology": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255"}], "value": "Single-pass type I membrane protein", "id": "SL-9905"}}]}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"}], "value": "Belongs to the CATSPERG family"}], "commentType": "SIMILARITY"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"}], "value": "In mouse, Slco6c1 is an additional auxiliary subunit of the CatSper complex. It is unclear if the related SLCO6A1 protein performs the same role in non-rodent species"}], "commentType": "CAUTION"}, {"commentType": "SEQUENCE CAUTION", "sequenceCautionType": "Erroneous initiation", "sequence": "BAC87333.1", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"}]}], "features": [{"type": "Signal", "location": {"start": {"value": 1, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 35, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255"}]}, {"type": "Chain", "location": {"start": {"value": 36, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 1159, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "Cation channel sperm-associated auxiliary subunit gamma", "featureId": "PRO_0000019565"}, {"type": "Topological domain", "location": {"start": {"value": 36, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 1065, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "Extracellular", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "C6KI89"}]}, {"